        "message": "Sensors override v3: try_to_lock the ECM-sync mutex \u2014 the acquisition itself was the remaining block\n\nsensors-override-pair-on-2 (extended override, both coupling waits\nnon-blocking) still tripped ONE ~103.4 ms physics stall at sim 41.5\n(dt_sim 2.0, frozen stamps, chain correctly expired). Root cause: the\nupdateTimeCv WAIT was gone but both it and the skip check live inside\nstd::unique_lock(renderUtilMutex) \u2014 and the render thread holds that\nmutex for the ENTIRE renderUtil.Update() (the slow scene/geometry\napplication at a viewpoint change). The physics thread blocked on the\nmutex ACQUISITION itself for exactly that duration.\n\nv3: try_to_lock. If the render thread holds the mutex, or the previous\nECM update is unconsumed, skip the cycle's UpdateFromECM entirely. The\nin-flight render keeps its buffered state; the next cycle refreshes.\nThe arming-side check (hunk D) stays on renderMutex, which the render\nthread holds only microseconds (its cv wait releases it)."
      },
